From 9f525e88e8a2d006c5d8e2a7792f19ed8f6f27be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zenium Upstream Port <upstream-port@zenium.invalid>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:07:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 82/88] cmdq: revert the partial vendor carry into the mailbox driver

Patch 0082 of this series. drivers-mailbox's mechanical carry (series commit 7836cbd3e) put +460
lines of the 4.19 vendor mailbox driver into mainline's mtk-cmdq-mailbox.c, +3 into
include/linux/mailbox/mtk-cmdq-mailbox.h and +2 into the directory Makefile. Those lines reference
cmdq_err, CMDQ_DRIVER_NAME, cmdq_msg and struct cmdq's base_pa member - engine-side names that
belong to vendor code this series does not carry - so enabling CONFIG_MTK_CMDQ_MBOX produced four
unresolved identifiers and the tree could not build the CMDQ path at all:

  drivers/mailbox/mtk-cmdq-mailbox.c:113: implicit declaration of 'cmdq_err'
  drivers/mailbox/mtk-cmdq-mailbox.c:690: 'CMDQ_DRIVER_NAME' undeclared
  drivers/mailbox/mtk-cmdq-mailbox.c:700: implicit declaration of 'cmdq_msg'
  drivers/mailbox/mtk-cmdq-mailbox.c:727: 'struct cmdq' has no member named 'base_pa'

Revert those three files to v5.15.220 so mainline's CMDQ stack is coherent again: one packet model,
one header, and drivers/mailbox/ + drivers/soc/mediatek/ compiling clean with
CONFIG_MTK_CMDQ_MBOX=y (measured: rc=0, mtk-cmdq-mailbox.o 123,688 B, mtk-cmdq-helper.o 92,776 B).
drivers/mailbox/mailbox.c deliberately keeps its +39-line delta - grepping that hunk for cmdq|gce is
empty, so it is a generic mailbox-core carry and unrelated to this incoherence.

include/linux/soc/mediatek/mtk-cmdq.h is untouched: it was never modified by the series, which is
why the collision was confined to the C files. The display path's remaining CMDQ needs are recorded
in the port report as a per-symbol contract rather than stubbed here.
